{
  "_about": "Component spec for pos-dialog (style/pos-dialog.css + views/partials/content/dialog.liquid + assets/js/pos-dialog.js). Built 2026-09-04 from the real, already-shipped CSS/JS — style/pos-dialog.css already existed (147 lines) before this spec, just never had a Tokens-panel spec, docs page, or nav wiring beyond a coming-soon badge placeholder. A real, pre-existing bug was found and fixed while building this: content/dialog.liquid's close button was missing the pos-close class that pos-dialog.css's own comment says provides its color/hover — without it the button had no color and no hover feedback at all. The docs preview cannot use the real showModal()/::backdrop (: static always-visible mockup, matching Popover's own precedent) — it renders the real .pos-dialog class and tokens with only the fixed/viewport-centering positioning neutralized (comp-dialog-demo-backdrop in styleguide.css, docs-only), and fakes the ::backdrop dimming with a plain div since a real ::backdrop only renders for a dialog opened via showModal(). The Default/Simple variant is layout-only (whether a title is shown) — it changes no token, only normal/hover/focus (the close button's own states) do. Two tokens have no Figma variable and are not silently invented: --pos-gap-section-elements (a literal 1rem value in pos-config.css, not routed through a primitive) and --pos-shadow-popover (aliases to --pos-primitive-shadow-layered, which itself has no Figma mapping). Regenerate spec-dialog.liquid via the Node regen snippet (RULES.md §6.4) if this file changes. All 11 real --pos-* custom properties in pos-dialog.css are documented, including two easy to miss because the docs preview never visually exercises them: --pos-color-page-background (only ever seen via the real ::backdrop, not this static mockup) and --pos-padding-page (only applies below a 500px viewport). --pos-transition-ui-detail is the one CSS variable intentionally excluded, matching the established convention across every other spec in this codebase of not documenting transition-timing tokens in the Tokens panel. 2026-09-04, caught via live review: (1) composedOf was wrongly left empty — the Default variant's own example content (Cancel/Confirm) uses real .pos-button instances, which RULES.md §7.12's own “practical check” explicitly calls out (composition can come from a component's own example content, not just its most obvious visual appearance) — this was an execution miss during the QA pass, not a missing rule; fixed to composedOf: [\"button\"]. (2) .pos-dialog had no border at all (relied solely on box-shadow) — added the same --pos-color-frame-transparent treatment as Card/Alert card/Toast. (3) .pos-dialog-actions used justify-content: center — changed to flex-end (buttons always right-aligned, primary action at the right edge — already the case since Cancel comes before Confirm in source order). (4) Real pre-existing bug caught live: the Simple variant's header used margin-block-end: -1rem (presumably meant to compensate for a taller title-bearing header, but wrongly applied even with no title), pulling the content paragraph up far enough to visually overlap the close icon — fixed to margin-block-end: 0. 2026-09-04, two more live-review fixes: (5) the title (.pos-heading-2, 32px/weight 500 by default) was resized to match the default Feature card title exactly (--pos-font-size-l/24px, weight 700, line-height 1.17). (6) the Simple (no-title) variant looked broken with the header-then-content stacking made obvious once the earlier overlap bug was fixed — restructured via .pos-dialog:has(.pos-dialog-header-simple) { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto } so the close button sits in its own right-aligned column beside the first line of content, instead of alone in a full-width row above it. 2026-09-04: after resizing the title to 24px, the header's old align-items: start plus a stale margin-block-start: -.3em (hand-tuned for the previous 32px size) made the title visually overflow above/below the header's own box instead of lining up with the close button — fixed to align-items: center on the header (robust regardless of exact font metrics) and removed the now-wrong negative margin entirely. 2026-09-04: replaced the CSS grid approach for the Simple variant (produced an extra empty row and a header box taller than the icon itself, confirmed via DevTools inspection) with a plain absolute-positioned corner button — content now starts at the very top of the dialog in line with the close button, and the button stays pinned top-right regardless of how many lines the content wraps to, since it is fully decoupled from document flow. 2026-09-04: composedOf also lists control-icons — the close (×) button composes the shared .pos-close component, which has its own dedicated spec/Tokens panel (control-icons.json); the color tokens stay directly listed here too since they drive this component's own Normal/Hover toggle, but composedOf now correctly points to where the icon's full detail (including states not relevant here) actually lives. 2026-09-04: found the actual root cause of the persistent Simple-variant misalignment — the content's first element (a <p>) carries the browser's own default top margin (pos-reset.css does not zero <p> margins), pushing its text below the absolutely-positioned close button's top edge; the button was never actually misplaced, the text was pushed down. Fixed with margin-block-start: 0 on the same rule that already reserves horizontal space for the button. 2026-09-04: replaced the absolute-positioned corner button for the Simple variant with a floated one (float: inline-end) after the absolute approach, though correct per the CSS spec's containing-block math, did not actually align in the browser (confirmed live, twice) — floating sidesteps that reasoning entirely by letting the browser's own text-wrapping engine position the content relative to the icon. 2026-09-04: matched the real Figma popup component (node 5767-76437) — supersedes fix (3) above: .pos-dialog-actions is left-aligned (justify-content: flex-start, not flex-end) with the primary button leftmost and secondary/Cancel to its right (button source order swapped to match); also added a divider (border-block-end: 1px solid --pos-color-frame) under the title+close row, with matching padding-block-end so the divider sits with even spacing above and below it, scoped only to the default (titled) header — the Simple variant's floated header has no full-width row to divide, so it explicitly resets padding/border/margin to none.",
  "component": "dialog",
  "name": "Dialog",
  "description": "A native, modal <dialog> window that dims and disables the rest of the page until the user confirms, cancels, or closes it.",
